```
Reason:
The absence of proper configuration for the TM QCN error event interrupts occurs because the interrupt type and FIFO interrupt enable settings are not being set when the event is enabled. This results in error events not being reported if they occur when the event is not enabled.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
desc.data[0] = cpu_to_le32(HCLGE_TM_QCN_ERR_INT_TYPE);
if (en) {
    desc.data[0] |= cpu_to_le32(HCLGE_TM_QCN_FIFO_INT_EN);
}
```
Reason:
These statements add the necessary configuration for the TM QCN error event interrupts by setting the interrupt type and enabling the FIFO interrupt when the event is enabled. This ensures that error events will be reported correctly when they occur.

